<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- superlooper unattended-debugger watchdog (issue #66). Fires `superlooper watchdog` every
     {interval_seconds} seconds as a scheduled ONE-SHOT — each firing reads the health signals
     (state/runner.heartbeat, state/ALERT, the no-progress shape), updates its episode state,
     and exits. NOT a keep-alive: no KeepAlive/RunAtLoad (issue #33's lesson stands — nothing
     under templates/ may keep a paneless daemon alive). This job MAY run under launchd because
     a check needs no cmux pane; only the rare launch step targets the RUNNER's recorded anchor
     pane (state/runner.anchor.json), and a launch that cannot resolve one fails LOUDLY into a
     journaled + notified outcome, never a fabricated success. Load it as a user LaunchAgent
     (~/Library/LaunchAgents) so notify/osascript run in the owner's GUI session; the one-time
     macOS permission that lets it text (notify.imessage_to) must be granted to that user, same
     as the nightly (plugin/skills/superlooper/references/runner-ops.md).

     PATH is explicit for the reason issue #306 measured: launchd hands a job only
     /usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin — no Homebrew, no ~/.local/bin — so a bare `gh` is not found.
     A watchdog without it still reads the heartbeat (a file) but every GitHub read refuses, which
     it correctly treats as UNOBSERVABLE and so freezes its clocks: the no-progress detector never
     fires, silently, on a job that looks perfectly healthy. Substitute the absolute dir THIS
     machine resolves gh in (`command -v gh`), ahead of launchd's own four. The `watchdog job`
     block of `superlooper doctor` in stack mode judges the installed job against exactly that
     (issue #328), and it judges what launchd is HOLDING — so editing this file changes nothing
     until the job is booted out and bootstrapped again.
     (Written the long way round because an XML comment may not contain a double hyphen, which is
     what a literal `doctor` flag would put here; the same trap this file already sprang once.)

     Placeholders ({label}, {superlooper_bin}, {repo_path}, {state_home}, {interval_seconds},
     {path}) are substituted literally. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>{label}</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>{superlooper_bin}</string>
        <string>watchdog</string>
        <string>--repo</string>
        <string>{repo_path}</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>{interval_seconds}</integer>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>{path}</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>{state_home}/logs/watchdog.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>{state_home}/logs/watchdog.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
